t></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO YUKIMASA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORITA AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OMOTO TOMOAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, YUKIMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORITA, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OMOTO, TOMOAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A molding powder for continuous casting of steel characterized in that it has a chemical composition comprising 25 to 70 wt % of SiO2, 10 to 50 wt % of CaO, 20 wt % or less of MgO and 0 to 2 wt % of F (inevitable impurities), and exhibits a melt viscosity at 1300  DEG C of 4 or more; and a method for continuous casting of steel using the molding powder.  The molding powder contains fluorine only in a small amount, which results in reducing the corrosion of a continuous casting installation and the fluorine content of waste water, and also allows the stable operation of a continuous casting process.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une poudre pour moulage d'acier par coulée continue. Cette poudre comprend une composition chimique contenant entre 25 et 70 % en poids de SiO2, entre 10 et 50 % en poids de CaO, au moins 20 % de MgO et entre 0 et 2 % en poids de F (impuretés inévitables). Par ailleurs, cette poudre présente à 1300  DEG C une viscosité à l'état fondu de 4 ou plus. L'invention concerne également une procédé de moulage par coulée continue faisant appel à cette poudre. Cette dernière contient du fluor en quantité réduite, ce qui permet de diminuer la corrosion d'une installation de coulée continue ainsi que la teneur en fluor des eaux usées et également d'obtenir un procédé de coulée continue à fonctionnement stable.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>